# Guided project setup for new users (`/iflow-setup`)

`/iflow-setup` takes a project from "I just installed issue-flow" to "I can start
working on issues". It checks what is missing — a Python project, a git repo, a
GitHub remote, GitHub CLI authentication, the issue-flow scaffold — and walks
through the gaps one confirmation at a time.

It handles both starting points:

- **A brand-new project** — an empty folder that needs `uv init`, `git init`,
  and a GitHub repository.
- **An existing project** — real code already, but something is missing.

This is an **off-path** command: `/iflow` never runs it for you. It is also not
the issue-capture step — that is `/iflow-init`.

